/**
 * @defgroup cfwx CFWx repository
 * @brief Educational numerical computation, model composition and execution lifecycle.
 * @details The CPU core uses owning row-major double arrays and explicit status
 * propagation. Experimental runners own datasets/model lifetimes and borrow named
 * logger contexts. CUDA is a distinct opt-in implementation; documentation
 * generation never configures or executes it.
 *
 * @defgroup core Core contracts
 * @ingroup cfwx
 * @brief Shared status codes, overflow checks and ownership rules.
 *
 * @defgroup containers Owning data structures
 * @ingroup core
 * @brief Vectors, matrices, tensors and affine neurons.
 * @details Initialize owners with zero, allocate through constructors, and release
 * through matching free functions. Shallow copies of live owners are invalid.
 *
 * @defgroup maths Mathematical primitives
 * @ingroup cfwx
 * @brief Stable activations, derivatives, losses and discounted returns.
 *
 * @defgroup activations Activations and derivatives
 * @ingroup maths
 * @brief ReLU, sigmoid, exact GELU, SiLU dispatch, tanh and softmax.
 *
 * @defgroup losses Losses and reductions
 * @ingroup maths
 * @brief Scalar and token-wise objectives with explicit mean-reduction gradients.
 *
 * @defgroup rewards Return computation
 * @ingroup maths
 * @brief Backward discounted-return recurrence with terminal bootstrap zero.
 *
 * @defgroup models Models and composition
 * @ingroup cfwx
 * @brief Dense projections, attention and Transformer building blocks.
 *
 * @defgroup dense Dense layers and SGD
 * @ingroup models
 * @brief Affine forward/backward operations and deterministic Xavier initialization.
 *
 * @defgroup attention Attention and normalization
 * @ingroup models
 * @brief Scaled dot products, causal/padding masks, LayerNorm and RMSNorm.
 *
 * @defgroup transformer Transformer building blocks
 * @ingroup models
 * @brief Embeddings, positions, residuals, dropout, FFNs and pre-normalized blocks.
 *
 * @defgroup training Analytic training
 * @ingroup models
 * @brief Local reverse-mode tape, gradient registries, clipping, AdamW and causal LM.
 * @details Recompute uses current parameters; do not mutate inputs or parameters
 * between the forward and corresponding backward computation. Fan-out sums all
 * parent adjoints, including Q/K/V and residual branches.
 *
 * @defgroup runtime Runtime lifecycle
 * @ingroup cfwx
 * @brief Token-weighted batching, full evaluation and incremental decoding.
 *
 * @defgroup checkpoint Checkpoint persistence
 * @ingroup runtime
 * @brief Versioned CPU parameter/optimizer/vocabulary/RNG persistence.
 * @details Publication uses a unique temporary, file fsync, rename and directory
 * fsync. Failure after rename can leave new contents visible without a durability
 * guarantee. This format is not interoperable with CUDA parameter storage.
 *
 * @defgroup gpu Optional CUDA backend
 * @ingroup cfwx
 * @brief Device reference execution and opt-in sequence-parallel launch fusion.
 * @warning GPU implementation has not been compiled or executed by the assistant.
 * No Tensor Core, cuBLAS or FlashAttention performance claim follows from source
 * presence. Manual validation instructions and design proposals are separate pages.
 *
 * @defgroup utilities Application utilities
 * @ingroup cfwx
 * @brief Legacy argument parsing, messages, ANSI colors and named logger injection.
 *
 * @defgroup logging Logging and injection
 * @ingroup utilities
 * @brief Borrowed experiment identity, independent levels and optional sinks.
 * @details The legacy backend uses shared FILE/localtime state and is not thread-safe.
 * Sinks must copy any message data they retain beyond a callback.
 *
 * @defgroup experiments Experimental runners
 * @ingroup cfwx
 * @brief Dataset/model orchestration with explicit cleanup and injected logging.
 *
 * @defgroup tests Tests and executable examples
 * @ingroup cfwx
 * @brief Reference, finite-difference, lifecycle, corruption and manual CUDA checks.
 * @details CPU checks run under Debug/Release and sanitizer builds. CUDA checks
 * are manually requested; generating their source pages does not execute them.
 *
 * @defgroup maintenance Build and maintenance tooling
 * @ingroup cfwx
 * @brief CMake integration, idempotent source scripts, editor files and CI workflows.
 */
